  "description": "Reid Comfort 1 ST | Comfort city bike\nComfortable, relaxed and easy to ride – a versatile comfort bike designed to make everyday cycling simple, enjoyable and accessible.\nThe Reid Bikes Comfort 1 ST features relaxed geometry that creates a comfortable, upright riding position, helping reduce fatigue and making it easier to enjoy longer rides. Comfort-focused components, including ergonomic handlebars, ergo grips and a comfort saddle, provide additional support whether you're riding around town, along cycle paths or enjoying a leisurely weekend ride.\nA Shimano 7-speed Revoshift drivetrain provides simple and reliable gear changes, while lightweight alloy V-brakes offer confident and controlled stopping.\nThe Comfort 1 ST rolls on 27.5\" double-wall alloy rims fitted with wide 2.35\" all-terrain tyres. The generous tyre width provides cushioning, grip and stability across roads, cycle paths and smoother mixed surfaces for a comfortable, smooth ride.\nWith its relaxed geometry, wide tyres, simple Shimano gearing and comfort-focused components, the Reid Comfort 1 ST is an easy and enjoyable choice for everyday journeys, leisure rides and anyone looking to get cycling with less effort.\nThe Reid Bikes Comfort 1 ST is ideal for:\n\nEveryday cycling – relaxed geometry and an upright riding position help make daily rides more comfortable\n\nCity and urban riding – stable 27.5\" wheels and wide tyres provide a smooth and controlled ride\n\nLeisurely rides – comfort-focused components help reduce fatigue on longer journeys\n\nCycle paths and mixed surfaces – 2.35\" all-terrain tyres provide cushioning, grip and stability\n\nSimple, reliable gearing – Shimano 7-speed Revoshift makes changing gears straightforward and intuitive\n\nComfort-focused riding – ergonomic handlebars, ergo grips and a comfort saddle provide additional support\n\nConfident stopping – lightweight alloy V-brakes deliver controlled and reliable braking\n\nAn upright riding position – relaxed geometry provides a comfortable and natural riding posture\n\nEveryday errands and weekend rides – a versatile, easy-going bike for getting around town or enjoying more miles at your own pace",
